# Step State Passing

OpenCTO does not pass business data between steps automatically.

**Same-run sharing** — write to `OPENCTO_WORKFLOW_RUN_ARTIFACTS_DIR/`:

```sh
mkdir -p "$OPENCTO_WORKFLOW_RUN_ARTIFACTS_DIR"
printf '{"result":"value"}\n' > "$OPENCTO_WORKFLOW_RUN_ARTIFACTS_DIR/payload.json"
```

Read from a later step in the same run:

```sh
cat "$OPENCTO_WORKFLOW_RUN_ARTIFACTS_DIR/payload.json"
```

**Cross-run persistence** — write and read under `OPENCTO_WORKFLOW_DATA_DIR/`. Each run starts with fresh process state; cross-run memory must be explicit file I/O. Always handle missing or invalid files gracefully.

---

# Runtime Environment Variables

Set by OpenCTO at step execution time. Do not hardcode their values in source files.

```
OPENCTO_WORKFLOWS_DIR              — root of all workflow source repos
                                     Each workflow: OPENCTO_WORKFLOWS_DIR/{workflow_id}/
                                     Read-only during step execution

OPENCTO_WORKFLOW_RUN_DIR           — current run snapshot and step working directory
                                     Runtime evidence only — not available to future runs

OPENCTO_WORKFLOW_RUN_ARTIFACTS_DIR — writable artifact directory for same-run step sharing
                                     Not available to future runs

OPENCTO_WORKFLOW_DATA_DIR          — persistent data directory for this workflow
                                     Git-ignored, writable at step runtime
                                     Survives WorkflowUpdate, deleted by WorkflowDelete
```

---

# Directory Layout

```
$OPENCTO_WORKSPACE/
  workflows/
    {workflow_id}/
      workflow.yml              <- manifest
      src/                      <- default location for implementation files
      data/                     <- persistent cross-run data, Git-ignored, do not author source here
      .git/                     <- do not edit, skip when searching
      .gitignore                <- managed by OpenCTO; append custom ignores only when necessary
  workflow-runs/                <- runtime snapshots, never edit
    {workflow_id}/
      {run_id}/
        workflow.yml
        src/
        artifacts/
```

Source is not limited to `src/`. Scripts, configs, and packages may live anywhere in the workflow directory unless the path is reserved or ignored.

